    "result": "I implemented `search_products` in `solution.py` and kept the signature and the `spec.md` rules. Validation comes first: `name_contains` must be a string, `limit` an integer from 1 to 100, `offset` an integer of at least 0 (booleans are rejected), and `order_by` must be exactly `\"name\"` or `\"price\"`, otherwise a `ValueError` is raised. The query always filters on `stock > 0`, adds an optional `price <= ?` clause when `max_price` is not `None`, and matches the name substring with `instr(lower(name), lower(?)) > 0`. That keeps `%` and `_` literal and makes matching case-insensitive for ASCII. Ordering uses a fixed column name chosen from a mapping (never user input), with `id ASC` as the tie-breaker, and `LIMIT`/`OFFSET` are bound as parameters. Results are dicts with only `id`, `name` and `price`. The only database operation is a single `SELECT`, so the database is never modified. I did not run or test the code, since shell access was unavailable and the task said not to.",
